{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch8E9d4FdpuMoChG2ysMj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review\n\nThe change replaces the per-view loop of `record_hit(&stats)` calls with a single `record_hits(&stats, u64::from(load.views))` call per worker. That is exactly what the description calls for.\n\n**Capabilities held**\n- `serve(tasks: &Tasks, load: &Load)` has the same signature as before. It holds only `Tasks` and uses it as it did: one `Shared` cell and one scope with one spawned worker per client. No narrowing changed.\n- `record_hits(stats: &Shared<Stats>, views: u64)` is private, like the `record_hit` it replaces. It takes no capability, only the shared cell it already had and a plain integer.\n\n**New uses of existing authority**\n- No new files, hosts, programs, environment variables, clock, randomness or stdin.\n- The number of tasks spawned is unchanged at `load.clients`. The only thing that changes is how often each task takes the lock.\n\n**Output sinks**\n- No `print!`, `println!`, `eprint!` or `eprintln!` calls are added. `serve` still returns the hit count to its caller, as before.\n\n**Public surface**\n- No new public items. `Load`, `ServeError` and `serve` are unchanged. `Stats` stays private.\n\nThe change only reorganizes in-memory locking inside capabilities the code already held. It takes no authority beyond what the description calls for.\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"approve\", \"findings\": []}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3278,"cache_read_input_tokens":1630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3278},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"408a76e8-e419-4a79-baa6-87